1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,750
Remove Element — LeetCode 27

2
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:04,600
Problem: remove every occurrence of val from nums, in place, and return k — how many remain.

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,900
Example: nums = [3, 2, 2, 3], val = 3

4
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:11,950
Result: k = 2, nums = [2, 2, …]; the rest is ignored

5
00:00:11,950 --> 00:00:15,950
Hint: don't erase — overwrite nums with the keepers, left to right

6
00:00:15,950 --> 00:00:20,700
Approach: two pointers — f (fast) reads every element, s (slow) marks the next write slot

7
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:24,800
Start: nums = [3, 2, 2, 3], val = 3; f and s both begin at 0

8
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,740
f = 0: nums[0] = 3

9
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:29,330
3 = val → skip; s stays

10
00:00:29,330 --> 00:00:31,270
f = 1: nums[1] = 2

11
00:00:31,270 --> 00:00:35,110
2 ≠ val → write it into slot s = 0

12
00:00:35,110 --> 00:00:37,050
f = 2: nums[2] = 2

13
00:00:37,050 --> 00:00:40,890
2 ≠ val → write it into slot s = 1

14
00:00:40,890 --> 00:00:42,830
f = 3: nums[3] = 3

15
00:00:42,830 --> 00:00:45,470
3 = val → skip

16
00:00:45,470 --> 00:00:49,310
Loop ends → k = s = 2

17
00:00:49,310 --> 00:00:52,860
The first k = 2 elements are the answer. Time O(n), space O(1)

18
00:00:52,860 --> 00:00:57,960
